WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.070
Most stories of a life begin with a birth.

2
00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:08.420
John's Gospel begins much earlier:
In the beginning was the Word.

3
00:00:08.470 --> 00:00:12.660
Those are the first words of the
Bible's opening book, Genesis.

4
00:00:12.710 --> 00:00:17.760
The Word, in Greek Logos,
is with God, and is God.

5
00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:21.500
So why begin the story
of Jesus before creation?

6
00:00:21.550 --> 00:00:25.370
In this mission, you'll read the
18 verses of John's Prologue,

7
00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:27.630
an overture to the whole Gospel.

8
00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:31.540
Then you'll follow two streams
of ideas behind the word Logos:

9
00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:33.800
one Jewish, one Greek.

10
00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:39.000
Your mission: find out why John starts
the story of Jesus before creation.
